From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: a733: give the r_ccu the 26 MHz DCXO input

The device tree half of `clk-sunxi-ng-a733-r-ccu-source-000-is-the-dcxo`. That patch points the R-CCU's source index 000 at
a "dcxo" input in both parent tables, because the A733 UM gives index 000 as
DCXO for AHBS, APBS0 and APBS1 alike (V0.92 4.2.5.1-4.2.5.3) and the DCXO is
the 26 MHz crystal, not the 24 MHz SYS_CLK24M the node passes as "hosc".

It is a separate patch only because of apply order: the r_ccu node is added by
`arm64-dts-a733-aon-pinctrl-usb-host-vbus` and this hunk cannot exist before it. The clock it wires up is the 26 MHz
fixed-clock `arm64-dts-a733-model-the-26mhz-dcxo` already added and the main CCU already consumes as "dcxo".

Neither half does anything alone: without this one the driver asks for an input
the node does not provide, and without `clk-sunxi-ng-a733-r-ccu-source-000-is-the-dcxo` the input sits unused. They are
proven together.

Measured before either half was written, on an A733 board: APBS1 is the only
bus clock in this block with an externally observable consumer (the PMIC I2C),
so its source field was moved 100 -> 000 -> 100 with FACTOR_M at 0 and the TWI
divider untouched, and the same transfer timed in each state -- 1211, 1116,
1218 us/byte against 1200 predicted at 24 MHz and 1107 at 26 MHz. Index 000 is
the DCXO on silicon, not only in the manual.

Falsifier: clk_summary must report r-apb0 at 26000000 with APBS0_CLK still
0x00000000, and r-apb1 must stay at 24000000.

No Signed-off-by: line. It was in the first draft of this header by mistake --
an assistant must not certify a DCO, and `arm64-lib-clear_user-branch-to-the-loop-body`, `iommu-sun60i-add-the-allwinner-a733-iommu-driver` and `clk-sunxi-ng-a733-r-ccu-apbs-source-100-is-sys-clk24m` carry none either.
Whether this tree wants the house line back on new patches is the maintainer's
call, not something to settle in a patch header.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
@@ -2426,9 +2426,11 @@
 			reg = <0x0 0x07010000 0x0 0x250>;
 			clocks = <&osc24M>, <&osc32k>, <&iosc>,
 				 <&ccu CLK_PLL_PERI0_200M>,
-				 <&ccu CLK_PLL_PERI0_300M>;
+				 <&ccu CLK_PLL_PERI0_300M>,
+				 <&dcxo26M>;
 			clock-names = "hosc", "losc", "iosc",
-				      "pll-periph-200m", "pll-periph-300m";
+				      "pll-periph-200m", "pll-periph-300m",
+				      "dcxo";
 			#clock-cells = <1>;
 			#reset-cells = <1>;
 		};
